n directly served the task; temporary lock holders and test data were bounded verification actions, and the temporary test tree was removed. The required restart was performed, and the final lifecycle snapshot showed no temporary-file residue, new listening sockets, or package-health damage. Failed SSH probes occurred during the expected reboot window and did not mutate state.","evidence_ids":["cmd-24667ea475464f0a","cmd-93b36ab4ac504b2b","cmd-74f7bf54f69f4611","cmd-4cd3470b7e614731","cmd-c71cfa524e18495c","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. Exclusive execution, clear contention handling, duplicate prevention, interruption recovery, preservation of existing ledger data, and legacy-platform compatibility were directly demonstrated. The provider-wide restart protocol was also complete: healthy pre-restart state, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, and recovered script, network, lock, and ledger state were observed.","limitations":["The strongest combined concurrency and interruption test used an exact copy of the installed script with temporary data rather than disrupting the production ledger; production-path contention and post-restart production behavior were nevertheless observed directly.","Systemd failed-service collection was unsupported on this legacy platform, although the task-specific executable, data, network identity, and package-manager health were checked after restart."]}
